{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1520357-dssy-do-super-science-yourself","id":1520357,"title":"DSSY! (Do Super Science Yourself!)","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","The Trinity Continuum"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-08-10T23:35:01-07:00","id":1520357,"title":"DSSY! (Do Super Science Yourself!)","content":"Inspired and powered characters are always capable of some super science creation, it\u2019s part of their nature, but it doesn\u2019t mean it\u2019s some easy task. The system to create your own super science is described in Trinity Continuum Core Rulebook, with some specific rules in Trinity Continuum: \u00c6on \u00c6xpansion and Trinity Continuum: Aberrant, but sometimes it is a bit too complex to understand, so to simplify the entire idea the step by step system is described below, similar to the character creation, but interacting with the character creation capacities, with some alterations due to the way the rules have changed in this book or to give it more predictable result.<br /> <br /> <b>Step 1: Concept</b><br /> The first thing that must be defined is what is the idea of the item, usually described in a very simple phase, like a screen to detect quantum sources, a tiara that increase the potency of Psionic powers or a freezing ray.<br /> <br /> <b>Step 2: Category</b><br /> It\u2019s fundamental to understand what the item is capable or not and also how it work in the hand of anyone, so it\u2019s important to define the category of the item, Advanced, Inspired or Powered item.<br /> The category is often limited by the character capacities, for example, Talents are incapable of creating Powered Super Science, and Assassins can only create Advanced items.<br /> <br /> <b>Step 3: Tags</b><br /> The only characteristic an item have is the tags, at least initially. Some tags open multiple options, and some define even more the way the items work, so it\u2019s important to define all the necessary tags to reach the desired result.<br /> <br /> <b>Step 4: Rank</b><br /> Once the tags are defined, the number of tags define the minimum rank of an item, usually the rank that the inventor will chose to use, as it is just easier to create the item of the lowest rank possible, but it\u2019s possible to give the item as a higher rank with no additional benefits.<br /> The item rank may be limited by the character capacities, usually a character can only create items of ranks equal or lower the character Science skill dots, for example.<br /> <br /> <b>Step 5: Constructing</b><br /> The character part of the process, the other steps being done by the player. According to the category, the character must go through a series of milestones, each of them taking some time.<br /> There are 5 different milestones that may or may not be part of the project, according to the category:<br /> <b>Research</b> is the milestone the character research the desired effects, be them Gifts or other powers.<br /> <b>Design</b> is the milestone the character creates the concept of the super science, it\u2019s parts, how the parts interact with each other and how to assembly them all together.<br /> <b>Special Materials Gathering</b> is the milestone the character collect the different special materials the character may require to create the super science.<br /> <b>Workshop Preparation</b> is the milestone the character set the place where the construction will take place, be it a mechanical workshop, a surgery room or a nuclear research facility, gathering the tools and common materials required.<br /> <b>Construction</b> is the final milestone, when the super science is finalized, be it constructed, born or summoned, according to the different project.<br /> Advanced Super Science requires 3 milestones, Design, Workshop Preparation and Construction.<br /> Inspired Super Science requires the 4 milestones, Design, Workshop Preparation, Special Materials Gathering and Construction.<br /> Powered Super Science requires each of the 5 milestones.<br /> How long each milestone takes to be complete is defined by the item complexity scale, as described ahead, and the difficulty of the roll related to the milestone itself is equal to the item rank. In addition to the milestones, all super science projects have a built in complication equal to its rank, that, if not bought will result in a Flaw of same rank, or a combination of flaws that total that rank, but the complication can be bought partially, resulting in a flaw of lower rank.<br /> While it may seam as a restricted process, each of the milestones can be as diverse as possible, the research milestone can vary from simple observation of the powers being used in the field to collecting samples of the subject to going to a library to find previous uses of that power in the literature.<br /> Different situations may require different Skills and Attributes, but the roll must be done by the end of the milestone to define the degree of success, in addition to any actions took during the process. This roll may also grant access to the Crafting Stunts, with many different options being available through the different books.<br /> A fail in the roll may result in a change in the way the character is approaching the current milestone, for example, while preparing a mechanical workshop for the project, the character may notice a failure in the way the pieces are made, and requiring a smith shop instead.<br /> Some stunts and character traits may remove entire milestones, for example using the On Time, Under Budget stunt, the character removes one milestone from the project entirely. The removed milestone may be specified by the stunt or trait, resulting in different explanations, from a research so well done that the design was already covered, to a innovative design that removed the need is special materials, for example.<br /> <br /> <b>Step 6: It\u2019s Ready</b><br /> Finally, if everything went all right, the item is ready to be used, just after the finish of the last milestone.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-11T16:52:49-07:00","id":1520418,"title":"","content":"Complexity scale defines how complex an item is, defining how hard it is to understand and construct the item. It\u2019s complexity scale is defined by its rank and category, rank 1 and 2 have complexity scale 0, rank 3 and 4 complexity scale 1 and rank 5 are complexity scale 2. Advanced Super Science causes no adjustments, Inspired Super Science increases the scale by 1 and Powered by 2.<br /> Repairing, reversing engineering or reforging an item reduces the complexity scale by 1, as the item being complete and possibly working helps the process of understanding and creating it.<br /> The resulting scale is compared to the creator mental scale to define the time it takes to cover a single milestone. If it\u2019s the same scale or lower, it takes a Turn to cover each milestone, 1 scale above takes a Shot, 2 scales above takes a Sequence, 3 scales above takes a Interlude, beyond 3 scales above the character can\u2019t work that milestone alone, requiring teams (and their powers of numbers) to reduce the scale gap.<br /> The actions related to the crafting are not meant to be exclusively taken on a workshop, so it may be interesting to have a shot of the character collecting materials, or a sequence of the character researching a library or taking classes with a professor in a university. The fact it happens on an accelerated time frame doesn't mean it need to be boring or ignored. It can happen after another scene, for example after making the place safe, the characters take some time to search for the research notes that represent the first milestone of a new project.<br /> The following are a list of the new time units in ascending order.<br /> <b>Shot:</b> This is the time between two scenes, time enough to rest for a moment, chat with the colleagues or fill the gas tank of a car. It takes from a few minutes to an hour, and is equivalent to a Scene. Any number of actions can be taken in a Shot.<br /> <b>Sequence: </b>This is a long period between events, enough to return to casual life, develop a new relationship, work on a big project. It takes several hours or even a few days, and is equivalent to a Session. Any number of Shots can be taken in a Sequence.<br /> <b>Interlude:</b> This is an extensive period of time, enough to learn new things, adapt to a new life, build the work of your life. It takes several days or even months, and its equivalent to a Chronicle. Any number of Sequences can be taken in a Interlude.<br /> <b>Hiatus: </b>This is a long time lapse, enough to see the world changing around you. It takes years or decades. Any number of Interludes can be taken in a Hiatus.<br /> <br /> <b>JURY RIGGING</b><br /> Jury rigging, described in Trinity Continuum Core Rulebook page 98, suffer an small change in how it works.<br /> Jury rigging is not about doing it fast, it\u2019s about using shortcuts to get a job done, reducing the complexity scale by 1 but creating a complication equal to item rank to the process, that if not bought off will turn into a flaw of same value.<br /> <br /> <b>OVERCLOCKING</b><br /> Overclocking, as Jury Rigging, suffers some changes on its working and result. Overclocking becomes a Stunt when repairing an item, what can be done even if the item is in good state. It makes it work better somehow, usually removing safety devices or adding more power when it should not fit, but becomes particularly risky.<br /> <i>OVERCLOCKING</i><br /> You add a special feature to the item, but it gets particularly unstable.<br /> System: For every 2 successes spent, add one point worth of tag to the item, but add the Unreliable flaw to it. If the item already have the Unreliable Flaw add the One-Time Use Flaw.\u200b","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-12T04:38:22-07:00","id":1520436,"title":"","content":"Thank you <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar24985_3.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"24985\" data-vbnamecard=\"24985\">Mateus Luz</a>! Finally I understand Super Science in <b>Trinity Continuum</b> and how it should be played! \ud83d\udc4f","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-12T05:49:04-07:00","id":1520441,"title":"","content":"It\u2019s not the original rules, it\u2019s a house rule from my book, but I want to let it free for people need a simpler way to play as inventors.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-12T09:50:21-07:00","id":1520458,"title":"","content":"<b>RANKS OF SUPER SCIENCE</b><br /> Super Science items have no cost, they are not available to sell in the open market. Some of the items are prototypes of the mundane items of the future, but it\u2019s probable that, due to the requirements to create or use it, these items will never be available to sell at all.<br /> The rank of a super science item works in a similar way to the cost of a mundane item, defining the number of tags the item may have. A rank 1 item may have up to 3 tags, a rank 2 may have up to 5 tags, a rank 3 may have up to 7 tags, a rank 4 up to 9 tags and a rank 5 up to 11 tags.<br /> Proxy tier psi users and Novas can create items of even higher ranks, but those items are far from being part of \u201cThe Basics\u201d.<br /> <br /> <b>CATEGORIES OF SUPER SCIENCE</b><br /> Super Science items are divided into 3 categories according to the how the items are dependents on inspired and powered characters, and into ranks, according to its complexity and general utility.<br /> The 3 categories, as described in Trinity Continuum Core Rulebook, are Advanced, Inspired and Powered.<br /> <br /> <b>ADVANCED DEVICES</b><br /> Advanced, being the most \u201ccommon kind\u201d, is the technology that is just a bit ahead of the setting standard, what ever the standard is. For example, in the 1930s a manned space rocket would be an Advanced item, as there are no working rockets at the time, and as it would take a few decades before they start to fly to the space, it would be a powerful item.<br /> Advanced super science can be created by any person, not requiring Inspiration, of course it would not be an easy task, but yet, given the proper tools and material anyone can move science forward, even if just a bit.<br /> Advanced items can use the common tags of the<br /> setting, but also tags not yet available at the time period, but these would cost more than what is expected in the future. The cost of the tag is increased by 1 if it would not be available for at least the next 20 years, increase by 2 if not available for at least the next 50 years and by 3 if not available for the next 100 years.<br /> Using the previous example, a rocket in the 1930s, using the Hybrid vehicle tag, that is avail- able about 30 years later, would cost 3 tags instead of 2 (other flight systems would still work).<br /> Additionally, Advanced Super Science also gains access to special tags, only available to Super Science items.<br /> <b>Quality (2-6):</b> Advanced items can have even higher enhancement that are not available to mundane items. The Quality tag may increase all the way to 6, granting its cost as enhancement.<br /> <b>Maneuverable (1-6):</b> Advanced vehicles can have even higher enhancement that are not avail- able to mundane vehicles. The Maneuverable tag may increase all the way to 6, granting its cost as enhancement.<br /> <b>Hard Armor (1-5):</b> Advanced armors can have even higher hard armor that are not available to\u200b mundane armors. The 5 dot version granting 3 condition boxes.<br /> <b>Soft Armor (1-5):</b> Advanced armors can have even higher soft armor that are not available to mundane armors. The cost of this tag is added to the cost of Inflict Injury stunt against the wearer.<br /> <b>Super Science (1-5):</b> The item gain access to a certain number of dots that can be spent on Edges. The number of dots is defined by the cost of the tag.<br /> 1 point: 1 dot of Edges<br /> 2 points: 3 dots of Edges<br /> 3 points: 5 dots of Edges<br /> 4 points: 7 dots of Edges<br /> 5 points: 10 dots of Edges<br /> <br /> <b>INSPIRED DEVICES</b><br /> Inspired super science is the material of real science fiction, it could maybe be replicated using sufficiently advanced technology, but it would not follow the same \u201crules\u201d as the Inspired item. For example, a Inspired super science energy generator that would not work according to the modern science, still it works as expected by the inventor, or even it could even produce one kind of energy that does not exist at all, at least by science.<br /> Inspired super science requires a Inspired or Powered inventor to create it, but, not even reverse engineering or the original project would allow a mundane scientist to replicate it. Other than that, the item works no matter who is using it.<br /> Beside the tags available to Advanced items, Inspired items can use part of the edge dots gained from the Super Science tag to gain Powered Edges. The following lines replace the equivalent lines on the tag described before.<br /> 3 points: 5 dots of Edges (up to 2 Powered)<br /> 4 points: 7 dots of Edges (up to 4 Powered)<br /> 5 points: 10 dots of Edges (up to 5 Powered)<br /> For example, a rank 2 item with the 3-points version of Super Science tag could have up to 5 dots of edges, of which up to 2 dots are of Powered Edges.\u200b","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-15T10:50:43-07:00","id":1520685,"title":"","content":"Thanks a lot for this threat Mateus, I already read these rules in your House rules the basics, it saved the crafting system for me and my players because we couldn't make heads or tails from it. That said, I'm really curious about how are they going to revamp it with the new supplement.<br /> If I may, can you make a similar post regarding equipment? Because that's another section that we're not clear about in some cases. For example, does a piece of equipment do anything beyond what its tags indicate? Do they give any enhancements just for using them for what they're been designed for? <br /> Thanks<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2964-firanai","name":"Firanai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2964_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"672"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-15T11:33:39-07:00","id":1520692,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Firanai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1520357-dssy-do-super-science-yourself?p=1520685#post1520685\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thanks a lot for this threat Mateus, I already read these rules in your House rules the basics, it saved the crafting system for me and my players because we couldn't make heads or tails from it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks!<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> That said, I'm really curious about how are they going to revamp it with the new supplement. </div> </div> </div>Actually I am planning on how to add the Adventure! Stunts and tags to this system (that are pretty close to Aether and Aegis\u2026 almost), as they add a lot of interesting things to the basics, like the option of changing a existent item, like improving your car instead of building a new one.<br /> I am not sure how much so far, but it is not too far from it to be fair. I have some nota, but I made them quite long time ago, so\u2026 but the first post, with the changed milestones is something I will add to the book soon, with other small corrections and word picking.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If I may, can you make a similar post regarding equipment? Because that's another section that we're not clear about in some cases. For example, does a piece of equipment do anything beyond what its tags indicate? Do they give any enhancements just for using them for what they're been designed for?<br /> Thanks </div> </div> </div>The idea is you only get what\u2019s on the tags, period. No extra enhancements (except that 1e that all weapons have). That\u2019s why I expanded the \u201cbasic tags\u201d beyond the mundane level, so you can have an item that grant a good enhancement, high soft and hard armor, etc. The number of tags also takes into account the need of enhancements <br /> If you use the Quality tag it grants enhancements to a tool or another equipment that perform specific actions, not only to attack actions. Much like the Maneuverable work for vehicles when you drive them (the action they are designed to).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}